    "english":  "I grieve in silence, and my golden bangles slip from my wasted wrists!\nDid she commit a grave fault in choosing to follow you\nthrough the desolate mountain pass where the fierce sun burns\nand the knobby jackfruit withers on its twisted branchΓÇö\nleaving behind her mother\u0027s grand house with its lofty grain-bins\nfilled with white unhusked rice that towered like mountain peaks?\nBe merciful to her, O traveler, for she has made you her sole refugeΓÇö\nthis tender maiden of sharp white teeth, whose golden skin is covered\nwith delicate beauty-spots, and whose thick dark tresses fall past her shoulders!",
